        "original_id": "b15425ba-0a9c-541a-9d44-6c01675a4584",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Todd Phillips, Scot Armstrong, Breckin Meyer, Seann William Scott, Paulo Costanzo, DJ Qualls, Avery Waddell\n- Works: Road Trip, Old School, Starsky & Hutch, The Hangover Trilogy, Due Date, War Dogs, In Too Deep, The New Guy, Inside Schwartz, Law & Order, Without a Trace, Angel\n- Organizations: NBC\n\nFacts:\n- In 2000, Todd Phillips wrote and directed the film \"Road Trip.\"\n- In 2000, \"Road Trip\" was an American comedy film directed by Todd Phillips and written by Scot Armstrong and Todd Phillips.\n- In 2000, \"Road Trip\" starred Breckin Meyer, Seann William Scott, Paulo Costanzo, and DJ Qualls as four college friends on an 1800-mile trip to recover an illicit tape mistakenly mailed to a girlfriend.\n- In 2001, NBC aired the American sitcom \"Inside Schwartz\" from September to December, and Breckin Meyer starred as the title character.\n- In 2003, Todd Phillips wrote and directed \"Old School.\"\n- In 2004, Todd Phillips wrote and directed \"Starsky & Hutch.\"\n- In 2009, 2011, and 2013, Todd Phillips wrote and directed \"The Hangover Trilogy.\"\n- In 2010, Todd Phillips wrote and directed \"Due Date.\"\n- In 2016, Todd Phillips wrote and directed \"War Dogs.\"\n- Avery Kidd Waddell is an American director, writer, and actor who appeared in the films \"In Too Deep,\" \"Road Trip,\" and \"The New Guy\" and guest-starred on \"Law & Order,\" \"Without a Trace,\" and \"Angel\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
